{
  "concept": "The shape of a hyperbola is entirely governed by a central guide rectangle whose dimensions determine the diagonal asymptotes the curves approach.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "x-axis and y-axis with arrowheads",
    "Center point at the origin (orange marker) with 'Center' label and leader line",
    "Two hyperbola branches opening left and right (solid dark blue)",
    "Transverse axis (solid red horizontal segment) with 'Transverse axis' label and leader line",
    "Conjugate axis (solid light blue vertical segment) with 'Conjugate axis' label and leader line",
    "Central guide rectangle (dashed teal box) passing through vertices and co-vertices",
    "Two asymptotes (dashed orange lines extending through origin and rectangle corners) with 'Asymptote' labels",
    "Two vertices (dark blue dots on x-axis) with 'Vertex' labels",
    "Two co-vertices (light blue dots on y-axis) with 'Co-vertex' labels",
    "Two foci (teal dots on x-axis outside vertices) with 'Focus' labels"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "transverseAxis",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Transverse axis length (a)",
      "range": [1, 5, 0.5],
      "default": 3,
      "teaches": "Varying 'a' moves the vertices along the x-axis, changing the width of the guide rectangle and setting where the hyperbola branches turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "conjugateAxis",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Conjugate axis length (b)",
      "range": [1, 5, 0.5],
      "default": 2,
      "teaches": "Varying 'b' changes the height of the guide rectangle without moving the vertices, which alters the slopes of the asymptotes and dictates how wide the hyperbola opens."
    },
    {
      "id": "guideToggle",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Construction Guides",
      "options": ["Show guides", "Hide guides"],
      "default": "Show guides",
      "teaches": "Toggling the guides off and on reveals that the hyperbola's branches are perfectly constrained by the invisible diagonals of the central rectangle."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The Transverse Axis",
      "narration": "The transverse axis (red) connects the two vertices. Its length determines the minimum distance between the two branches of the hyperbola.",
      "state": { "transverseAxis": 4, "conjugateAxis": 2, "guideToggle": "Show guides" }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Conjugate Axis",
      "narration": "Increase the conjugate axis (blue). The vertices don't move, but the central rectangle gets taller, steepening the asymptotes and causing the hyperbola to open wider.",
      "state": { "transverseAxis": 4, "conjugateAxis": 4, "guideToggle": "Show guides" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Asymptotic Bounds",
      "narration": "Without the guide rectangle and asymptotes visible, it is hard to see why the hyperbola curves exactly as it does. The construction guides are the hidden scaffold of the shape.",
      "state": { "transverseAxis": 4, "conjugateAxis": 4, "guideToggle": "Hide guides" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The \"openness\" of a hyperbola isn't arbitrary; it perfectly hugs the diagonal lines extending from a simple rectangle built from the transverse and conjugate axes.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Center the diagram at the origin (0,0). Use precise coloring to separate concepts: red for the transverse axis (which maps to real intersections), light blue for the conjugate axis/co-vertices (imaginary intersections), teal dashed lines for the guide rectangle, and orange dashed for asymptotes. Foci must be calculated dynamically as c = sqrt(a^2 + b^2). Labels should feature thin black leader lines pointing exactly to their respective geometric components. When 'Hide guides' is selected, make the rectangle, asymptotes, and conjugate/transverse axis segments invisible, leaving only the axes, hyperbola curves, and foci."
